      "## create\n\n`client.airspaceControlOrders.create(classificationMarking: string, dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE', opExName: string, originator: string, source: string, startTime: string, id?: string, acoComments?: string, acoSerialNum?: string, airspaceControlMeansStatus?: { airspaceControlMeans?: { airspaceControlPoint?: object[]; airspaceTimePeriod?: object[]; bearing0?: number; bearing1?: number; cmId?: string; cmShape?: 'POLYARC' | '1TRACK' | 'POLYGON' | 'CIRCLE' | 'CORRIDOR' | 'APOINT' | 'AORBIT' | 'GEOLINE'; cmType?: string; cntrlAuth?: string; cntrlAuthFreqs?: string[]; coord0?: string; coord1?: string; corrWayPoints?: string[]; effVDim?: string; freeText?: string; genTextInd?: string; geoDatumAlt?: string; link16Id?: string; orbitAlignment?: string; polyCoord?: string[]; radMag0?: number; radMag1?: number; radMagUnit?: string; trackLeg?: number; transAltitude?: string; usage?: string; width?: number; widthLeft?: number; widthRight?: number; widthUnit?: string; }[]; cmStat?: string; cmStatId?: string[]; }[], airspaceControlOrderReferences?: { refOriginator?: string; refSerialNum?: string; refSICs?: string[]; refSId?: string; refSpecialNotation?: string; refTs?: string; refType?: string; }[], areaOfValidity?: string, classReasons?: string[], classSource?: string, declassExemptionCodes?: string[], downgradeInsDates?: string[], geoDatum?: string, month?: string, opExInfo?: string, opExInfoAlt?: string, origin?: string, planOrigNum?: string, qualifier?: string, qualSN?: number, serialNum?: string, stopQualifier?: string, stopTime?: string, undLnkTrks?: string[]): void`\n\n**post** `/udl/airspacecontrolorder`\n\nService operation to take a single AirspaceControlOrder record as a POST body and ingest into the database. A specific role is required to perform this service operation. Please contact the UDL team for assistance.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `classificationMarking: string`\n  Classification marking of the data in IC/CAPCO Portion-marked format.\n\n- `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  Indicator of whether the data is REAL, TEST, EXERCISE, or SIMULATED data:\n\nREAL: Data collected or produced that pertains to real-world objects, events, and analysis.\n\nTEST: Specific datasets used to evaluate compliance with specifications and requirements, and for validating technical, functional, and performance characteristics.\n\nEXERCISE: Data pertaining to a government or military exercise. The data may include both real and simulated data.\n\nSIMULATED: Synthetic data generated by a model to mimic real-world datasets.\n\n- `opExName: string`\n  Specifies the unique operation or exercise name, nickname, or codeword assigned to a joint exercise or operation plan.\n\n- `originator: string`\n  The identifier of the originator of this message.\n\n- `source: string`\n  Source of the data.\n\n- `startTime: string`\n  The start of the effective time period of this airspace control order, in ISO 8601 UTC format with millisecond precision.\n\n- `id?: string`\n  Unique identifier of the record, auto-generated by the system.\n\n- `acoComments?: string`\n  Free text information expressed in natural language.\n\n- `acoSerialNum?: string`\n  The serial number of this airspace control order.\n\n- `airspaceControlMeansStatus?: { airspaceControlMeans?: { airspaceControlPoint?: { ctrlPtAltitude?: string; ctrlPtLocation?: string; ctrlPtName?: string; ctrlPtType?: string; }[]; airspaceTimePeriod?: { intDur?: string[]; intFreq?: string[]; timeEnd?: string; timeMode?: string; timeStart?: string; }[]; bearing0?: number; bearing1?: number; cmId?: string; cmShape?: 'POLYARC' | '1TRACK' | 'POLYGON' | 'CIRCLE' | 'CORRIDOR' | 'APOINT' | 'AORBIT' | 'GEOLINE'; cmType?: string; cntrlAuth?: string; cntrlAuthFreqs?: string[]; coord0?: string; coord1?: string; corrWayPoints?: string[]; effVDim?: string; freeText?: string; genTextInd?: string; geoDatumAlt?: string; link16Id?: string; orbitAlignment?: string; polyCoord?: string[]; radMag0?: number; radMag1?: number; radMagUnit?: string; trackLeg?: number; transAltitude?: string; usage?: string; width?: number; widthLeft?: number; widthRight?: number; widthUnit?: string; }[]; cmStat?: string; cmStatId?: string[]; }[]`\n  Mandatory nested segment to report multiple airspace control means statuses within an ACOID.\n\n- `airspaceControlOrderReferences?: { refOriginator?: string; refSerialNum?: string; refSICs?: string[]; refSId?: string; refSpecialNotation?: string; refTs?: string; refType?: string; }[]`\n  The airspaceControlReferences set provides both USMTF and non-USMTF references for this airspace control order.\n\n- `areaOfValidity?: string`\n  Name of the area of the command for which the ACO is valid.\n\n- `classReasons?: string[]`\n  Mandatory if classSource uses the \"IORIG\" designator. Must be a REASON FOR CLASSIFICATION code.\n\n- `classSource?: string`\n  Markings defining the source material or the original classification authority for the ACO message.\n\n- `declassExemptionCodes?: string[]`\n  Coded entries that provide justification for exemption from automatic downgrading or declassification of the airspace control order.\n\n- `downgradeInsDates?: string[]`\n  Markings providing the literal guidance or date for downgrading or declassifying the airspace control order.\n\n- `geoDatum?: string`\n  Specifies the geodetic datum by which the spatial coordinates of the controlled airspace are calculated.\n\n- `month?: string`\n  The month in which the message originated.\n\n- `opExInfo?: string`\n  Supplementary name that can be used to further identify exercise nicknames, or to provide the primary nickname of the option or the alternative of an operational plan.\n\n- `opExInfoAlt?: string`\n  The secondary supplementary nickname of the option or the alternative of the operational plan or order.\n\n- `origin?: string`\n  Originating system or organization which produced the data, if different from the source. The origin may be different than the source if the source was a mediating system which forwarded the data on behalf of the origin system. If null, the source may be assumed to be the origin.\n\n- `planOrigNum?: string`\n  The official identifier of the military establishment responsible for the operation plan and the identification number assigned to this plan.\n\n- `qualifier?: string`\n  The qualifier which caveats the message status.\n\n- `qualSN?: number`\n  The serial number associated with the message qualifier.\n\n- `serialNum?: string`\n  The unique message identifier sequentially assigned by the originator.\n\n- `stopQualifier?: string`\n  A qualifier for the end of the effective time period of this airspace control order, such as AFTER, ASOF, NLT, etc. Used with field stopTime to indicate a relative time.\n\n- `stopTime?: string`\n  The end of the effective time period of this airspace control order, in ISO 8601 UTC format with millisecond precision.\n\n- `undLnkTrks?: string[]`\n  Array of unique link 16 identifiers that will be assigned to a future airspace control means.\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nawait client.airspaceControlOrders.create({\n  classificationMarking: 'U',\n  dataMode: 'TEST',\n  opExName: 'DESERT WIND',\n  originator: 'USCENTCOM',\n  source: 'Bluestaq',\n  startTime: '2024-01-07T13:55:43.123Z',\n})\n```",
