      "## update\n\n`client.channels.update(id: string, classificationMarking: string, dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE', idTransponder: string, name: string, source: string, id?: string, apid?: string, beamName?: string, compression?: string, encryption?: string, idBeam?: string, idRFBand?: string, origin?: string, owner?: string, pkg?: string, res?: string, sid?: string, type?: string, vpid?: string): void`\n\n**put** `/udl/channel/{id}`\n\nService operation to update a single Channel. A Comm payload may have multiple transponders and a transponder may have many channels. A specific role is required to perform this service operation. Please contact the UDL team for assistance.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `id: string`\n\n- `classificationMarking: string`\n  Classification marking of the data in IC/CAPCO Portion-marked format.\n\n- `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  Indicator of whether the data is REAL, TEST, EXERCISE, or SIMULATED data:\n\nREAL: Data collected or produced that pertains to real-world objects, events, and analysis.\n\nTEST: Specific datasets used to evaluate compliance with specifications and requirements, and for validating technical, functional, and performance characteristics.\n\nEXERCISE: Data pertaining to a government or military exercise. The data may include both real and simulated data.\n\nSIMULATED: Synthetic data generated by a model to mimic real-world datasets.\n\n- `idTransponder: string`\n  ID of the parent transponder object for this Channel.\n\n- `name: string`\n  Channel name.\n\n- `source: string`\n  Source of the data.\n\n- `id?: string`\n  Unique identifier of the record, auto-generated by the system.\n\n- `apid?: string`\n  Channel aPid.\n\n- `beamName?: string`\n  The antenna beam ID of the particular beam for this channel.  beamName is not unique across payloads.\n\n- `compression?: string`\n  Channel compression.\n\n- `encryption?: string`\n  Channel encryption.\n\n- `idBeam?: string`\n  Identifier of the particular beam for this channel.\n\n- `idRFBand?: string`\n  ID of the RF Band object for this channel.\n\n- `origin?: string`\n  Originating system or organization which produced the data, if different from the source. The origin may be different than the source if the source was a mediating system which forwarded the data on behalf of the origin system. If null, the source may be assumed to be the origin.\n\n- `owner?: string`\n  Owner.\n\n- `pkg?: string`\n  Pkg.\n\n- `res?: string`\n  Res.\n\n- `sid?: string`\n  SID.\n\n- `type?: string`\n  Channel type.\n\n- `vpid?: string`\n  Channel vPid.\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nawait client.channels.update('id', {\n  classificationMarking: 'U',\n  dataMode: 'TEST',\n  idTransponder: 'REF-TRANSPONDER-ID',\n  name: 'Example name',\n  source: 'system.source',\n})\n```",
