    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.deconflictset.history.list(eventStartTime: string, columns?: string, firstResult?: number, maxResults?: number): { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; eventStartTime: string; numWindows: number; source: string; id?: string; calculationEndTime?: string; calculationId?: string; calculationStartTime?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; deconflictWindows?: object[]; errors?: string[]; eventEndTime?: string; eventType?: string; idLaserDeconflictRequest?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; referenceFrame?: string; sourceDL?: string; tags?: string[]; transactionId?: string; warnings?: string[]; }`\n\n**get** `/udl/deconflictset/history`\n\nService operation to dynamically query historical data by a variety of query parameters not specified in this API documentation. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid/required query parameter information.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `eventStartTime: string`\n  The start time of the event associated with the set of DeconflictWindow records, in ISO 8601 UTC format with millisecond precision. (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.sssZ)\n\n- `columns?: string`\n  optional, fields for retrieval. When omitted, ALL fields are assumed. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid query fields that can be selected.\n\n- `firstResult?: number`\n\n- `maxResults?: number`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; eventStartTime: string; numWindows: number; source: string; id?: string; calculationEndTime?: string; calculationId?: string; calculationStartTime?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; deconflictWindows?: { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; eventStartTime: string; source: string; startTime: string; stopTime: string; id?: string; angleOfEntry?: number; angleOfExit?: number; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; entryCoords?: number[]; eventType?: string; exitCoords?: number[]; idDeconflictSet?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; sourceDL?: string; target?: string; targetType?: string; victim?: string; windowType?: string; }[]; errors?: string[]; eventEndTime?: string; eventType?: string; idLaserDeconflictRequest?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; referenceFrame?: string; sourceDL?: string; tags?: string[]; transactionId?: string; warnings?: string[]; }`\n  The DeconflictSet service provides access to a set of DeconflictWindows and metadata about those data. A DeconflictWindow describes a time window during which an action, such as target engagement, may either occur or is prohibited from occurring. The DeconflictWindow model includes information about the spatial details for specific target types. A flag is provided to specify whether the window should be associated with taking action (OPEN), or if no action should occur (CLOSED).\n\n  - `classificationMarking: string`\n  - `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  - `eventStartTime: string`\n  - `numWindows: number`\n  - `source: string`\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `calculationEndTime?: string`\n  - `calculationId?: string`\n  - `calculationStartTime?: string`\n  - `createdAt?: string`\n  - `createdBy?: string`\n  - `deconflictWindows?: { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; eventStartTime: string; source: string; startTime: string; stopTime: string; id?: string; angleOfEntry?: number; angleOfExit?: number; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; entryCoords?: number[]; eventType?: string; exitCoords?: number[]; idDeconflictSet?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; sourceDL?: string; target?: string; targetType?: string; victim?: string; windowType?: string; }[]`\n  - `errors?: string[]`\n  - `eventEndTime?: string`\n  - `eventType?: string`\n  - `idLaserDeconflictRequest?: string`\n  - `origin?: string`\n  - `origNetwork?: string`\n  - `referenceFrame?: string`\n  - `sourceDL?: string`\n  - `tags?: string[]`\n  - `transactionId?: string`\n  - `warnings?: string[]`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const historyListResponse of client.deconflictset.history.list({ eventStartTime: '2019-12-27T18:11:19.117Z' })) {\n  console.log(historyListResponse);\n}\n```",
