    markdown:
      "## unvalidated_publish\n\n`client.ecpedr.unvalidatedPublish(body: { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; ecpedrMeasurements: { obType: string; obUoM: string; chanEnergyHigh?: number; chanEnergyLow?: number; chanId?: string; chanType?: string; chanUnit?: string; msgNumber?: number; obQuality?: string; obQualityIndicator?: string; obValue?: number; species?: string; }[]; obTime: string; source: string; id?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; genSystem?: string; genTime?: string; idOnOrbit?: string; idSensor?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; origObjectId?: string; origSensorId?: string; satNo?: number; senPos?: number[]; senReferenceFrame?: 'J2000' | 'EFG/TDR' | 'ECR/ECEF' | 'TEME' | 'ITRF' | 'GCRF'; sourceDL?: string; tags?: string[]; transactionId?: string; }[]): void`\n\n**post** `/filedrop/udl-ecpedr`\n\nService operation to take multiple ECPEDR records as a POST body and ingest into the database. This operation is intended to be used for automated feeds into UDL. A specific role is required to perform this service operation. Please contact the UDL team for assistance.\n\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `body: { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; ecpedrMeasurements: { obType: string; obUoM: string; chanEnergyHigh?: number; chanEnergyLow?: number; chanId?: string; chanType?: string; chanUnit?: string; msgNumber?: number; obQuality?: string; obQualityIndicator?: string; obValue?: number; species?: string; }[]; obTime: string; source: string; id?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; genSystem?: string; genTime?: string; idOnOrbit?: string; idSensor?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; origObjectId?: string; origSensorId?: string; satNo?: number; senPos?: number[]; senReferenceFrame?: 'J2000' | 'EFG/TDR' | 'ECR/ECEF' | 'TEME' | 'ITRF' | 'GCRF'; sourceDL?: string; tags?: string[]; transactionId?: string; }[]`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nawait client.ecpedr.unvalidatedPublish({ body: [{\n  classificationMarking: 'U',\n  dataMode: 'TEST',\n  ecpedrMeasurements: [{ obType: 'FLUX', obUoM: '#/MeV/cm^2/sr/s' }],\n  obTime: '2025-03-13T17:00:00.123456Z',\n  source: 'Bluestaq',\n}] })\n```",
