      "## unvalidated_publish\n\n`client.effectRequests.unvalidatedPublish(body: { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; effectList: string[]; source: string; id?: string; context?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; deadlineType?: string; endTime?: string; externalRequestId?: string; metricTypes?: string[]; metricWeights?: number[]; modelClass?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; priority?: string; startTime?: string; state?: string; targetSrcId?: string; targetSrcType?: string; }[]): void`\n\n**post** `/filedrop/udl-effectrequest`\n\nService operation to take multiple EffectRequests as a POST body and ingest into the database. This operation is intended to be used for automated feeds into UDL. A specific role is required to perform this service operation. Please contact the UDL team for assistance.\n\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `body: { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; effectList: string[]; source: string; id?: string; context?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; deadlineType?: string; endTime?: string; externalRequestId?: string; metricTypes?: string[]; metricWeights?: number[]; modelClass?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; priority?: string; startTime?: string; state?: string; targetSrcId?: string; targetSrcType?: string; }[]`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nawait client.effectRequests.unvalidatedPublish({ body: [{\n  classificationMarking: 'U',\n  dataMode: 'TEST',\n  effectList: ['COVER', 'DECEIVE'],\n  source: 'Bluestaq',\n}] })\n```",
