    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.effectRequests.history.list(createdAt: string, columns?: string, firstResult?: number, maxResults?: number): { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; effectList: string[]; source: string; id?: string; context?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; deadlineType?: string; endTime?: string; externalRequestId?: string; metricTypes?: string[]; metricWeights?: number[]; modelClass?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; priority?: string; startTime?: string; state?: string; targetSrcId?: string; targetSrcType?: string; }`\n\n**get** `/udl/effectrequest/history`\n\nService operation to dynamically query historical data by a variety of query parameters not specified in this API documentation. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid/required query parameter information.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `createdAt: string`\n  Time the row was created in the database, auto-populated by the system. (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.sssZ)\n\n- `columns?: string`\n  optional, fields for retrieval. When omitted, ALL fields are assumed. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid query fields that can be selected.\n\n- `firstResult?: number`\n\n- `maxResults?: number`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; effectList: string[]; source: string; id?: string; context?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; deadlineType?: string; endTime?: string; externalRequestId?: string; metricTypes?: string[]; metricWeights?: number[]; modelClass?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; priority?: string; startTime?: string; state?: string; targetSrcId?: string; targetSrcType?: string; }`\n  A request for various effects on a target.\n\n  - `classificationMarking: string`\n  - `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  - `effectList: string[]`\n  - `source: string`\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `context?: string`\n  - `createdAt?: string`\n  - `createdBy?: string`\n  - `deadlineType?: string`\n  - `endTime?: string`\n  - `externalRequestId?: string`\n  - `metricTypes?: string[]`\n  - `metricWeights?: number[]`\n  - `modelClass?: string`\n  - `origin?: string`\n  - `origNetwork?: string`\n  - `priority?: string`\n  - `startTime?: string`\n  - `state?: string`\n  - `targetSrcId?: string`\n  - `targetSrcType?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const historyListResponse of client.effectRequests.history.list({ createdAt: '2019-12-27' })) {\n  console.log(historyListResponse);\n}\n```",
