    markdown:
      "## create_bulk\n\n`client.elsets.createBulk(body: { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; epoch: string; source: string; agom?: number; algorithm?: string; apogee?: number; argOfPerigee?: number; ballisticCoeff?: number; bStar?: number; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; descriptor?: string; eccentricity?: number; ephemType?: number; idElset?: string; idOnOrbit?: string; idOrbitDetermination?: string; inclination?: number; line1?: string; line2?: string; meanAnomaly?: number; meanMotion?: number; meanMotionDDot?: number; meanMotionDot?: number; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; origObjectId?: string; perigee?: number; period?: number; raan?: number; rawFileURI?: string; revNo?: number; satNo?: number; semiMajorAxis?: number; sourcedData?: string[]; sourcedDataTypes?: 'EO' | 'RADAR' | 'RF' | 'DOA' | 'ELSET' | 'SV'[]; sourceDL?: string; tags?: string[]; transactionId?: string; uct?: boolean; }[], dupeCheck?: boolean): void`\n\n**post** `/udl/elset/createBulk`\n\nService operation intended for initial integration only, to take a list of elsets as a POST body and ingest into the database with or without dupe detection. Default is no dupe checking. This operation is not intended to be used for automated feeds into UDL. Data providers should contact the UDL team for specific role assignments and for instructions on setting up a permanent feed through an alternate mechanism.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `body: { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; epoch: string; source: string; agom?: number; algorithm?: string; apogee?: number; argOfPerigee?: number; ballisticCoeff?: number; bStar?: number; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; descriptor?: string; eccentricity?: number; ephemType?: number; idElset?: string; idOnOrbit?: string; idOrbitDetermination?: string; inclination?: number; line1?: string; line2?: string; meanAnomaly?: number; meanMotion?: number; meanMotionDDot?: number; meanMotionDot?: number; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; origObjectId?: string; perigee?: number; period?: number; raan?: number; rawFileURI?: string; revNo?: number; satNo?: number; semiMajorAxis?: number; sourcedData?: string[]; sourcedDataTypes?: 'EO' | 'RADAR' | 'RF' | 'DOA' | 'ELSET' | 'SV'[]; sourceDL?: string; tags?: string[]; transactionId?: string; uct?: boolean; }[]`\n\n- `dupeCheck?: boolean`\n  Boolean indicating if these elsets should be checked for duplicates, default is not to.\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nawait client.elsets.createBulk({ body: [{\n  classificationMarking: 'U',\n  dataMode: 'TEST',\n  epoch: '2018-01-01T16:00:00.123456Z',\n  source: 'Bluestaq',\n}] })\n```",
