    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.ephemeris.attitudeData.list(asId: string, firstResult?: number, maxResults?: number): { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; source: string; ts: string; id?: string; asId?: string; coningAngle?: number; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; declination?: number; idOnOrbit?: string; motionType?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; origObjectId?: string; precPeriod?: number; q1?: number; q1Dot?: number; q2?: number; q2Dot?: number; q3?: number; q3Dot?: number; qc?: number; qcDot?: number; ra?: number; satNo?: number; spinPeriod?: number; xAngle?: number[]; xRate?: number[]; yAngle?: number[]; yRate?: number[]; zAngle?: number[]; zRate?: number[]; }`\n\n**get** `/udl/attitudedata`\n\nService operation to dynamically query data by a variety of query parameters not specified in this API documentation. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid/required query parameter information.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `asId: string`\n  Unique identifier of the parent AttitudeSet associated with this record. (uuid)\n\n- `firstResult?: number`\n\n- `maxResults?: number`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; source: string; ts: string; id?: string; asId?: string; coningAngle?: number; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; declination?: number; idOnOrbit?: string; motionType?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; origObjectId?: string; precPeriod?: number; q1?: number; q1Dot?: number; q2?: number; q2Dot?: number; q3?: number; q3Dot?: number; qc?: number; qcDot?: number; ra?: number; satNo?: number; spinPeriod?: number; xAngle?: number[]; xRate?: number[]; yAngle?: number[]; yRate?: number[]; zAngle?: number[]; zRate?: number[]; }`\n  These services provide operations for posting and querying attitude of on-orbit objects.  Attitude describes the orientation of an object, which can be represented by quaternions or euler angles.  The AttitudeSet ID (asId) identifies the 'AttitudeSet' record which contains details of the underlying data as well as a collection of attitude points. Points must be retrieved by first identifying a desired AttitudeSet and pulling its points by that AttitudeSet ID 'asId'.\n\n  - `classificationMarking: string`\n  - `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  - `source: string`\n  - `ts: string`\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `asId?: string`\n  - `coningAngle?: number`\n  - `createdAt?: string`\n  - `createdBy?: string`\n  - `declination?: number`\n  - `idOnOrbit?: string`\n  - `motionType?: string`\n  - `origin?: string`\n  - `origNetwork?: string`\n  - `origObjectId?: string`\n  - `precPeriod?: number`\n  - `q1?: number`\n  - `q1Dot?: number`\n  - `q2?: number`\n  - `q2Dot?: number`\n  - `q3?: number`\n  - `q3Dot?: number`\n  - `qc?: number`\n  - `qcDot?: number`\n  - `ra?: number`\n  - `satNo?: number`\n  - `spinPeriod?: number`\n  - `xAngle?: number[]`\n  - `xRate?: number[]`\n  - `yAngle?: number[]`\n  - `yRate?: number[]`\n  - `zAngle?: number[]`\n  - `zRate?: number[]`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const attitudeDataAbridged of client.ephemeris.attitudeData.list({ asId: 'asId' })) {\n  console.log(attitudeDataAbridged);\n}\n```",
