    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.eventEvolution.list(eventId?: string, firstResult?: number, maxResults?: number, startTime?: string): { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; eventId: string; source: string; startTime: string; summary: string; id?: string; agjson?: string; andims?: number; asrid?: number; atext?: string; atype?: string; category?: string; countryCode?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; dataDescription?: string; endTime?: string; geoAdminLevel1?: string; geoAdminLevel2?: string; geoAdminLevel3?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; redact?: boolean; srcIds?: string[]; srcTyps?: string[]; status?: string; tags?: string[]; url?: string[]; }`\n\n**get** `/udl/eventevolution`\n\nService operation to dynamically query data by a variety of query parameters not specified in this API documentation. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid/required query parameter information.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `eventId?: string`\n  (One or more of fields 'eventId, startTime' are required.) User-provided unique identifier of this activity or event. This ID should remain the same on subsequent updates in order to associate all records pertaining to the activity or event.\n\n- `firstResult?: number`\n\n- `maxResults?: number`\n\n- `startTime?: string`\n  (One or more of fields 'eventId, startTime' are required.) The actual or estimated start time of the activity or event, in ISO 8601 UTC format. (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.sssZ)\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; eventId: string; source: string; startTime: string; summary: string; id?: string; agjson?: string; andims?: number; asrid?: number; atext?: string; atype?: string; category?: string; countryCode?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; dataDescription?: string; endTime?: string; geoAdminLevel1?: string; geoAdminLevel2?: string; geoAdminLevel3?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; redact?: boolean; srcIds?: string[]; srcTyps?: string[]; status?: string; tags?: string[]; url?: string[]; }`\n  Event Evolution is a unique service supporting the association of UDL records of various data types to a common event or activity. The associations may be a one time summary, aggregating sources of a past event, or of an ongoing activity that evolves over a period of time.\n\n  - `classificationMarking: string`\n  - `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  - `eventId: string`\n  - `source: string`\n  - `startTime: string`\n  - `summary: string`\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `agjson?: string`\n  - `andims?: number`\n  - `asrid?: number`\n  - `atext?: string`\n  - `atype?: string`\n  - `category?: string`\n  - `countryCode?: string`\n  - `createdAt?: string`\n  - `createdBy?: string`\n  - `dataDescription?: string`\n  - `endTime?: string`\n  - `geoAdminLevel1?: string`\n  - `geoAdminLevel2?: string`\n  - `geoAdminLevel3?: string`\n  - `origin?: string`\n  - `origNetwork?: string`\n  - `redact?: boolean`\n  - `srcIds?: string[]`\n  - `srcTyps?: string[]`\n  - `status?: string`\n  - `tags?: string[]`\n  - `url?: string[]`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const eventEvolutionListResponse of client.eventEvolution.list()) {\n  console.log(eventEvolutionListResponse);\n}\n```",
