    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.featureAssessment.history.list(idAnalyticImagery: string, columns?: string, firstResult?: number, maxResults?: number): { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; featureTs: string; featureUoM: string; idAnalyticImagery: string; source: string; id?: string; agjson?: string; andims?: number; annLims?: number[][]; annText?: string[]; area?: string; asrid?: number; assessment?: string; atext?: string; atype?: string; confidence?: number; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; externalId?: string; featureArray?: number[]; featureBool?: boolean; featureString?: string; featureStringArray?: string[]; featureValue?: number; heading?: number; height?: number; length?: number; name?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; sourceDL?: string; speed?: number; srcIds?: string[]; srcTs?: string[]; srcTyps?: string[]; tags?: string[]; transactionId?: string; type?: string; width?: number; }`\n\n**get** `/udl/featureassessment/history`\n\nService operation to dynamically query historical data by a variety of query parameters not specified in this API documentation. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid/required query parameter information.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `idAnalyticImagery: string`\n  Unique identifier of the Analytic Imagery associated with this Feature Assessment record.\n\n- `columns?: string`\n  optional, fields for retrieval. When omitted, ALL fields are assumed. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid query fields that can be selected.\n\n- `firstResult?: number`\n\n- `maxResults?: number`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; featureTs: string; featureUoM: string; idAnalyticImagery: string; source: string; id?: string; agjson?: string; andims?: number; annLims?: number[][]; annText?: string[]; area?: string; asrid?: number; assessment?: string; atext?: string; atype?: string; confidence?: number; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; externalId?: string; featureArray?: number[]; featureBool?: boolean; featureString?: string; featureStringArray?: string[]; featureValue?: number; heading?: number; height?: number; length?: number; name?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; sourceDL?: string; speed?: number; srcIds?: string[]; srcTs?: string[]; srcTyps?: string[]; tags?: string[]; transactionId?: string; type?: string; width?: number; }`\n  Feature assessments obtained from imagery analysis or other data analytics. Feature assessments are georeferenced terrestrial features such as marine vessels, vehicles, buildings, etc., or contain other types of non terrestrial assessments such as spacecraft structures. Geospatial queries are supported through either the regionText (WKT) or regionGeoJSON fields.\n\n  - `classificationMarking: string`\n  - `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  - `featureTs: string`\n  - `featureUoM: string`\n  - `idAnalyticImagery: string`\n  - `source: string`\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `agjson?: string`\n  - `andims?: number`\n  - `annLims?: number[][]`\n  - `annText?: string[]`\n  - `area?: string`\n  - `asrid?: number`\n  - `assessment?: string`\n  - `atext?: string`\n  - `atype?: string`\n  - `confidence?: number`\n  - `createdAt?: string`\n  - `createdBy?: string`\n  - `externalId?: string`\n  - `featureArray?: number[]`\n  - `featureBool?: boolean`\n  - `featureString?: string`\n  - `featureStringArray?: string[]`\n  - `featureValue?: number`\n  - `heading?: number`\n  - `height?: number`\n  - `length?: number`\n  - `name?: string`\n  - `origin?: string`\n  - `origNetwork?: string`\n  - `sourceDL?: string`\n  - `speed?: number`\n  - `srcIds?: string[]`\n  - `srcTs?: string[]`\n  - `srcTyps?: string[]`\n  - `tags?: string[]`\n  - `transactionId?: string`\n  - `type?: string`\n  - `width?: number`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const historyListResponse of client.featureAssessment.history.list({ idAnalyticImagery: 'idAnalyticImagery' })) {\n  console.log(historyListResponse);\n}\n```",
