    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.groundImagery.history.list(imageTime: string, columns?: string, firstResult?: number, maxResults?: number): { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; filename: string; imageTime: string; source: string; id?: string; checksumValue?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; filesize?: number; format?: string; idSensor?: string; keywords?: string[]; name?: string; notes?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; origSensorId?: string; region?: string; regionGeoJSON?: string; regionNDims?: number; regionSRid?: number; regionText?: string; regionType?: string; sourceDL?: string; subjectId?: string; tags?: string[]; transactionId?: string; updatedAt?: string; updatedBy?: string; }`\n\n**get** `/udl/groundimagery/history`\n\nService operation to dynamically query historical data by a variety of query parameters not specified in this API documentation. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid/required query parameter information.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `imageTime: string`\n  Timestamp the image was captured/produced. (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.ssssssZ)\n\n- `columns?: string`\n  optional, fields for retrieval. When omitted, ALL fields are assumed. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid query fields that can be selected.\n\n- `firstResult?: number`\n\n- `maxResults?: number`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; filename: string; imageTime: string; source: string; id?: string; checksumValue?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; filesize?: number; format?: string; idSensor?: string; keywords?: string[]; name?: string; notes?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; origSensorId?: string; region?: string; regionGeoJSON?: string; regionNDims?: number; regionSRid?: number; regionText?: string; regionType?: string; sourceDL?: string; subjectId?: string; tags?: string[]; transactionId?: string; updatedAt?: string; updatedBy?: string; }`\n  Imagery of terrestrial regions from on-orbit, air, and other sensors.\n\n  - `classificationMarking: string`\n  - `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  - `filename: string`\n  - `imageTime: string`\n  - `source: string`\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `checksumValue?: string`\n  - `createdAt?: string`\n  - `createdBy?: string`\n  - `filesize?: number`\n  - `format?: string`\n  - `idSensor?: string`\n  - `keywords?: string[]`\n  - `name?: string`\n  - `notes?: string`\n  - `origin?: string`\n  - `origNetwork?: string`\n  - `origSensorId?: string`\n  - `region?: string`\n  - `regionGeoJSON?: string`\n  - `regionNDims?: number`\n  - `regionSRid?: number`\n  - `regionText?: string`\n  - `regionType?: string`\n  - `sourceDL?: string`\n  - `subjectId?: string`\n  - `tags?: string[]`\n  - `transactionId?: string`\n  - `updatedAt?: string`\n  - `updatedBy?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const historyListResponse of client.groundImagery.history.list({ imageTime: '2019-12-27T18:11:19.117Z' })) {\n  console.log(historyListResponse);\n}\n```",
