    markdown:
      "## get\n\n`client.hazard.get(id: string, firstResult?: number, maxResults?: number): { alarms: string[]; alarmValues: number[]; classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; detectTime: string; detectType: string; source: string; id?: string; a?: number; activity?: number; bottleId?: string; casRN?: string; channel?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; ctrnTime?: number; density?: number; dep?: number; depCtrn?: number; dose?: number; doseRate?: number; duration?: number; gBar?: number; harmful?: boolean; hBar?: number; idPOI?: string; idTrack?: string; massFrac?: number; matCat?: number; matClass?: string; matName?: string; matType?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; ppm?: number; radCtrn?: number; readings?: string[]; readingUnits?: string[]; readingValues?: number[]; z?: number; }`\n\n**get** `/udl/hazard/{id}`\n\nService operation to get a single Hazard by its unique ID passed as a path parameter.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `id: string`\n\n- `firstResult?: number`\n\n- `maxResults?: number`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ alarms: string[]; alarmValues: number[]; classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; detectTime: string; detectType: string; source: string; id?: string; a?: number; activity?: number; bottleId?: string; casRN?: string; channel?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; ctrnTime?: number; density?: number; dep?: number; depCtrn?: number; dose?: number; doseRate?: number; duration?: number; gBar?: number; harmful?: boolean; hBar?: number; idPOI?: string; idTrack?: string; massFrac?: number; matCat?: number; matClass?: string; matName?: string; matType?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; ppm?: number; radCtrn?: number; readings?: string[]; readingUnits?: string[]; readingValues?: number[]; z?: number; }`\n  Hazard contains information concerning the exposure of a geographic area to a Chemical, Biological, Radiological, or Nuclear (CBRN) contaminant. The Hazard schema includes the detection time and type of contamination as well as optional information regarding specific material properties, the extent of contamination, and identification of affected regions.\n\n  - `alarms: string[]`\n  - `alarmValues: number[]`\n  - `classificationMarking: string`\n  - `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  - `detectTime: string`\n  - `detectType: string`\n  - `source: string`\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `a?: number`\n  - `activity?: number`\n  - `bottleId?: string`\n  - `casRN?: string`\n  - `channel?: string`\n  - `createdAt?: string`\n  - `createdBy?: string`\n  - `ctrnTime?: number`\n  - `density?: number`\n  - `dep?: number`\n  - `depCtrn?: number`\n  - `dose?: number`\n  - `doseRate?: number`\n  - `duration?: number`\n  - `gBar?: number`\n  - `harmful?: boolean`\n  - `hBar?: number`\n  - `idPOI?: string`\n  - `idTrack?: string`\n  - `massFrac?: number`\n  - `matCat?: number`\n  - `matClass?: string`\n  - `matName?: string`\n  - `matType?: string`\n  - `origin?: string`\n  - `origNetwork?: string`\n  - `ppm?: number`\n  - `radCtrn?: number`\n  - `readings?: string[]`\n  - `readingUnits?: string[]`\n  - `readingValues?: number[]`\n  - `z?: number`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nconst hazard = await client.hazard.get('id');\n\nconsole.log(hazard);\n```",
