    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.itemTrackings.history.list(ts: string, columns?: string, firstResult?: number, maxResults?: number): { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; scanCode: string; scannerId: string; source: string; ts: string; id?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; dvCode?: string; idItem?: string; keys?: string[]; lat?: number; lon?: number; notes?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; scanType?: string; scGenTool?: string; sourceDL?: string; type?: string; values?: string[]; }`\n\n**get** `/udl/itemtracking/history`\n\nService operation to dynamically query historical data by a variety of query parameters not specified in this API documentation. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid/required query parameter information.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `ts: string`\n  The timestamp of the scan, in ISO 8601 UTC format with millisecond precision. (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.sssZ)\n\n- `columns?: string`\n  optional, fields for retrieval. When omitted, ALL fields are assumed. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid query fields that can be selected.\n\n- `firstResult?: number`\n\n- `maxResults?: number`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; scanCode: string; scannerId: string; source: string; ts: string; id?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; dvCode?: string; idItem?: string; keys?: string[]; lat?: number; lon?: number; notes?: string; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; scanType?: string; scGenTool?: string; sourceDL?: string; type?: string; values?: string[]; }`\n\n  - `classificationMarking: string`\n  - `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  - `scanCode: string`\n  - `scannerId: string`\n  - `source: string`\n  - `ts: string`\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `createdAt?: string`\n  - `createdBy?: string`\n  - `dvCode?: string`\n  - `idItem?: string`\n  - `keys?: string[]`\n  - `lat?: number`\n  - `lon?: number`\n  - `notes?: string`\n  - `origin?: string`\n  - `origNetwork?: string`\n  - `scanType?: string`\n  - `scGenTool?: string`\n  - `sourceDL?: string`\n  - `type?: string`\n  - `values?: string[]`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const historyListResponse of client.itemTrackings.history.list({ ts: '2019-12-27T18:11:19.117Z' })) {\n  console.log(historyListResponse);\n}\n```",
