      "## list\n\n`client.location.list(firstResult?: number, maxResults?: number): { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; name: string; source: string; altitude?: number; countryCode?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; idLocation?: string; lat?: number; lon?: number; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; }`\n\n**get** `/udl/location`\n\nService operation to dynamically query data by a variety of query parameters not specified in this API documentation. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid/required query parameter information.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `firstResult?: number`\n\n- `maxResults?: number`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; name: string; source: string; altitude?: number; countryCode?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; idLocation?: string; lat?: number; lon?: number; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; }`\n  Model representation of a location, which is a specific fixed point on the earth and is used to denote the locations of fixed sensors, operating units, etc.\n\n  - `classificationMarking: string`\n  - `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  - `name: string`\n  - `source: string`\n  - `altitude?: number`\n  - `countryCode?: string`\n  - `createdAt?: string`\n  - `createdBy?: string`\n  - `idLocation?: string`\n  - `lat?: number`\n  - `lon?: number`\n  - `origin?: string`\n  - `origNetwork?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const locationAbridged of client.location.list()) {\n  console.log(locationAbridged);\n}\n```",
