      "## create\n\n`client.onorbitlist.create(classificationMarking: string, dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE', name: string, onOrbitListItems: { clearingBoxCrossTrack?: number; clearingBoxInTrack?: number; clearingRadius?: number; commonName?: string; countryCode?: string; expiredOn?: string; freqMins?: number; monitoringType?: string; objectId?: string; orbitRegime?: string; origObjectId?: string; payloadPriority?: number; rank?: number; urgency?: number; }[], source: string, id?: string, defaultRevisitRateMins?: number, description?: string, listPriority?: number, namespace?: string, origin?: string, tags?: string[], transactionId?: string): void`\n\n**post** `/udl/onorbitlist`\n\nService operation to take a single OnOrbitList as a POST body and ingest into the database. A specific role is required to perform this service operation. Please contact the UDL team for assistance.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `classificationMarking: string`\n  Classification marking of the data in IC/CAPCO Portion-marked format.\n\n- `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  Indicator of whether the data is REAL, TEST, EXERCISE, or SIMULATED data:\n\nREAL: Data collected or produced that pertains to real-world objects, events, and analysis.\n\nTEST: Specific datasets used to evaluate compliance with specifications and requirements, and for validating technical, functional, and performance characteristics.\n\nEXERCISE: Data pertaining to a government or military exercise. The data may include both real and simulated data.\n\nSIMULATED: Synthetic data generated by a model to mimic real-world datasets.\n\n- `name: string`\n  Unique name of the list.\n\n- `onOrbitListItems: { clearingBoxCrossTrack?: number; clearingBoxInTrack?: number; clearingRadius?: number; commonName?: string; countryCode?: string; expiredOn?: string; freqMins?: number; monitoringType?: string; objectId?: string; orbitRegime?: string; origObjectId?: string; payloadPriority?: number; rank?: number; urgency?: number; }[]`\n  This is a list of onOrbitListItems that will be related one-to-one with an onOrbit entry.\n\n- `source: string`\n  Source of the data.\n\n- `id?: string`\n  Unique identifier of the record, auto-generated by the system.\n\n- `defaultRevisitRateMins?: number`\n  Default revisit rate in minutes for all objects in this list.\n\n- `description?: string`\n  Description of the list.\n\n- `listPriority?: number`\n  Numerical priority of this orbit list relative to other orbit lists; lower values indicate higher priority. Decimal values allowed for fine granularity.  Consumers should contact the provider for details on the priority.\n\n- `namespace?: string`\n  Defined naming system that ensures each satellite or space object has a unique and unambiguous identifier within the name space (e.g. JCO, 18SDS). If null, it is assumed to be 18th Space Defense Squadron (18SDS).\n\n- `origin?: string`\n  Originating system or organization which produced the data, if different from the source. The origin may be different than the source if the source was a mediating system which forwarded the data on behalf of the origin system. If null, the source may be assumed to be the origin.\n\n- `tags?: string[]`\n  Optional array of provider/source specific tags for this data, where each element is no longer than 32 characters, used for implementing data owner conditional access controls to restrict access to the data. Should be left null by data providers unless conditional access controls are coordinated with the UDL team.\n\n- `transactionId?: string`\n  Optional identifier to track a commercial or marketplace transaction executed to produce this data.\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nawait client.onorbitlist.create({\n  classificationMarking: 'U',\n  dataMode: 'TEST',\n  name: 'HRR-SATELLITES',\n  onOrbitListItems: [{}],\n  source: 'Bluestaq',\n})\n```"