    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.onorbitthrusterstatus.create(classificationMarking: string, dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE', idOnorbitThruster: string, source: string, statusTime: string, id?: string, estDeltaV?: number, fuelMass?: number, fuelMassUnc?: number, isp?: number, maxDeltaV?: number, minDeltaV?: number, name?: string, operational?: boolean, origin?: string, propMassAvg?: number, propMassMax?: number, propMassMedian?: number, propMassMin?: number, thrustMax?: number, totalDeltaV?: number): void`\n\n**post** `/udl/onorbitthrusterstatus`\n\nService operation to take a single OnorbitThrusterStatus record as a POST body and ingest into the database. A specific role is required to perform this service operation. Please contact the UDL team for assistance.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `classificationMarking: string`\n  Classification marking of the data in IC/CAPCO Portion-marked format.\n\n- `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  Indicator of whether the data is REAL, TEST, EXERCISE, or SIMULATED data:\n\nREAL: Data collected or produced that pertains to real-world objects, events, and analysis.\n\nTEST: Specific datasets used to evaluate compliance with specifications and requirements, and for validating technical, functional, and performance characteristics.\n\nEXERCISE: Data pertaining to a government or military exercise. The data may include both real and simulated data.\n\nSIMULATED: Synthetic data generated by a model to mimic real-world datasets.\n\n- `idOnorbitThruster: string`\n  ID of the associated OnorbitThruster record. This ID can be used to obtain additional information on an onorbit thruster object using the 'get  by ID' operation (e.g. /udl/onorbitthruster/{id}). For example, the OnorbitThruster object with idOnorbitThruster = abc would be queried as /udl/onorbitthruster/abc.\n\n- `source: string`\n  Source of the data.\n\n- `statusTime: string`\n  Datetime of the thruster status observation in ISO 8601 UTC datetime format with millisecond precision.\n\n- `id?: string`\n  Unique identifier of the record, auto-generated by the system.\n\n- `estDeltaV?: number`\n  Estimated available delta-velocity for this thruster, in meters per second.\n\n- `fuelMass?: number`\n  Total fuel mass available for this thruster's type, in kilograms.\n\n- `fuelMassUnc?: number`\n  1-sigma uncertainty of the total fuel mass available for this thruster type, in kilograms.\n\n- `isp?: number`\n  Specific impulse for this thruster, in seconds.\n\n- `maxDeltaV?: number`\n  Maximum available delta-velocity for this thruster, in meters per second.\n\n- `minDeltaV?: number`\n  Minimum available delta-velocity for this thruster, in meters per second.\n\n- `name?: string`\n  Identifier of this thruster.\n\n- `operational?: boolean`\n  Flag indicating if this thruster is operational.\n\n- `origin?: string`\n  Originating system or organization which produced the data, if different from the source. The origin may be different than the source if the source was a mediating system which forwarded the data on behalf of the origin system. If null, the source may be assumed to be the origin.\n\n- `propMassAvg?: number`\n  Average available propellant mass for this thruster's type, in kilograms.\n\n- `propMassMax?: number`\n  Maximum available propellant mass for this thruster's type, in kilograms.\n\n- `propMassMedian?: number`\n  Median available propellant mass for this thruster's type, in kilograms.\n\n- `propMassMin?: number`\n  Minimum available propellant mass for this thruster's type, in kilograms.\n\n- `thrustMax?: number`\n  Maximum available thrust for this thruster, in newtons.\n\n- `totalDeltaV?: number`\n  Total delta-velocity available for this thruster's type, in meters per second.\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nawait client.onorbitthrusterstatus.create({\n  classificationMarking: 'U',\n  dataMode: 'TEST',\n  idOnorbitThruster: 'ff7dc909-e8b4-4a54-8529-1963d4e9b353',\n  source: 'Bluestaq',\n  statusTime: '2024-01-01T16:00:00.123Z',\n})\n```",
