    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.seraDataEarlyWarning.create(classificationMarking: string, dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE', source: string, spacecraftId: string, id?: string, bestResolution?: number, earthPointing?: boolean, frequencyLimits?: string, groundStationLocations?: string, groundStations?: string, hostedForCompanyOrgId?: string, idIR?: string, manufacturerOrgId?: string, missileLaunchPhaseDetectionAbility?: string, name?: string, origin?: string, partnerSpacecraftId?: string, payloadNotes?: string, spectralBands?: string): void`\n\n**post** `/udl/seradataearlywarning`\n\nService operation to take a single SeradataEarlyWarning as a POST body and ingest into the database. A specific role is required to perform this service operation. Please contact the UDL team for assistance.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `classificationMarking: string`\n  Classification marking of the data in IC/CAPCO Portion-marked format.\n\n- `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  Indicator of whether the data is REAL, TEST, EXERCISE, or SIMULATED data:\n\nREAL: Data collected or produced that pertains to real-world objects, events, and analysis.\n\nTEST: Specific datasets used to evaluate compliance with specifications and requirements, and for validating technical, functional, and performance characteristics.\n\nEXERCISE: Data pertaining to a government or military exercise. The data may include both real and simulated data.\n\nSIMULATED: Synthetic data generated by a model to mimic real-world datasets.\n\n- `source: string`\n  Source of the data.\n\n- `spacecraftId: string`\n  Seradata ID of the spacecraft (SeradataSpacecraftDetails ID).\n\n- `id?: string`\n  Unique identifier of the record, auto-generated by the system.\n\n- `bestResolution?: number`\n  Best resolution for this IR in meters.\n\n- `earthPointing?: boolean`\n  Is the sensor Earth Pointing.\n\n- `frequencyLimits?: string`\n  Frequency Limits for this IR.\n\n- `groundStationLocations?: string`\n  Ground Station Locations for this IR.\n\n- `groundStations?: string`\n  Ground Station info for this IR.\n\n- `hostedForCompanyOrgId?: string`\n  Hosted for company/Organization Id.\n\n- `idIR?: string`\n  UUID of the parent IR record.\n\n- `manufacturerOrgId?: string`\n  Manufacturer Organization Id.\n\n- `missileLaunchPhaseDetectionAbility?: string`\n  Missile Launch Phase Detection Ability.\n\n- `name?: string`\n  Sensor name from Seradata, e.g. Infra red telescope, Schmidt Telescope, etc.\n\n- `origin?: string`\n  Originating system or organization which produced the data, if different from the source. The origin may be different than the source if the source was a mediating system which forwarded the data on behalf of the origin system. If null, the source may be assumed to be the origin.\n\n- `partnerSpacecraftId?: string`\n  Seradata ID of the spacecraft (SeradataSpacecraftDetails ID).\n\n- `payloadNotes?: string`\n  Payload notes.\n\n- `spectralBands?: string`\n  Spectral Bands, e.g. Infra-Red.\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nawait client.seraDataEarlyWarning.create({\n  classificationMarking: 'U',\n  dataMode: 'TEST',\n  source: 'Bluestaq',\n  spacecraftId: 'spacecraftId',\n})\n```",
