    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.seradataRadarPayload.create(classificationMarking: string, dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE', source: string, spacecraftId: string, id?: string, bandwidth?: number, bestResolution?: number, category?: string, constellationInterferometricCapability?: string, dutyCycle?: string, fieldOfRegard?: number, fieldOfView?: number, frequency?: number, frequencyBand?: string, groundStationLocations?: string, groundStations?: string, hostedForCompanyOrgId?: string, idSensor?: string, manufacturerOrgId?: string, name?: string, notes?: string, origin?: string, partnerSpacecraft?: string, pointingMethod?: string, receivePolarization?: string, recorderSize?: string, swathWidth?: number, transmitPolarization?: string, waveLength?: number): void`\n\n**post** `/udl/seradataradarpayload`\n\nService operation to take a single SeradataRadarPayload as a POST body and ingest into the database. A specific role is required to perform this service operation. Please contact the UDL team for assistance.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `classificationMarking: string`\n  Classification marking of the data in IC/CAPCO Portion-marked format.\n\n- `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  Indicator of whether the data is REAL, TEST, EXERCISE, or SIMULATED data:\n\nREAL: Data collected or produced that pertains to real-world objects, events, and analysis.\n\nTEST: Specific datasets used to evaluate compliance with specifications and requirements, and for validating technical, functional, and performance characteristics.\n\nEXERCISE: Data pertaining to a government or military exercise. The data may include both real and simulated data.\n\nSIMULATED: Synthetic data generated by a model to mimic real-world datasets.\n\n- `source: string`\n  Source of the data.\n\n- `spacecraftId: string`\n  Seradata ID of the spacecraft (SeradataSpacecraftDetails ID).\n\n- `id?: string`\n  Unique identifier of the record, auto-generated by the system.\n\n- `bandwidth?: number`\n  Radar bandwidth in mega hertz.\n\n- `bestResolution?: number`\n  Best resolution in meters.\n\n- `category?: string`\n  Radar category, e.g. SAR, Surface Search, etc.\n\n- `constellationInterferometricCapability?: string`\n  Constellation interferometric capability.\n\n- `dutyCycle?: string`\n  Duty cycle.\n\n- `fieldOfRegard?: number`\n  Field of regard of this radar in degrees.\n\n- `fieldOfView?: number`\n  Field of view of this radar in kilometers.\n\n- `frequency?: number`\n  Frequency in giga hertz.\n\n- `frequencyBand?: string`\n  Name of the band of this RF range (e.g. X,K,Ku,Ka,L,S,C,UHF,VHF,EHF,SHF,UNK,VLF,HF,E,Q,V,W). See RFBandType for more details and descriptions of each band name.\n\n- `groundStationLocations?: string`\n  Ground Station Locations for this payload.\n\n- `groundStations?: string`\n  Ground Station info for this payload.\n\n- `hostedForCompanyOrgId?: string`\n  Hosted for company/Organization Id.\n\n- `idSensor?: string`\n  UUID of the Sensor record.\n\n- `manufacturerOrgId?: string`\n  Manufacturer Organization Id.\n\n- `name?: string`\n  Sensor name from Seradata, e.g. ALT (Radar Altimeter), COSI (Corea SAR Instrument), etc.\n\n- `notes?: string`\n  Payload notes.\n\n- `origin?: string`\n  Originating system or organization which produced the data, if different from the source. The origin may be different than the source if the source was a mediating system which forwarded the data on behalf of the origin system. If null, the source may be assumed to be the origin.\n\n- `partnerSpacecraft?: string`\n  Partner seradata-spacecraft.\n\n- `pointingMethod?: string`\n  Point method for this radar, e.g. Spacecraft.\n\n- `receivePolarization?: string`\n  Receive polarization, e.g. Lin Dual, Lin vert, etc.\n\n- `recorderSize?: string`\n  Recorder size, e.g. 256.\n\n- `swathWidth?: number`\n  Swath width in kilometers.\n\n- `transmitPolarization?: string`\n  Transmit polarization, e.g. Lin Dual, Lin vert, etc.\n\n- `waveLength?: number`\n  Wave length in meters.\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nawait client.seradataRadarPayload.create({\n  classificationMarking: 'U',\n  dataMode: 'TEST',\n  source: 'Bluestaq',\n  spacecraftId: '12345',\n})\n```",
