    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.trackRoute.create(classificationMarking: string, dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE', lastUpdateDate: string, source: string, type: string, id?: string, altitudeBlocks?: { altitudeSequenceId?: string; lowerAltitude?: number; upperAltitude?: number; }[], apnSetting?: string, apxBeaconCode?: string, artccMessage?: string, creatingOrg?: string, direction?: string, effectiveDate?: string, externalId?: string, lastUsedDate?: string, locationTrackId?: string, origin?: string, poc?: { office?: string; phone?: string; pocName?: string; pocOrg?: string; pocSequenceId?: number; pocTypeName?: string; rank?: string; remark?: string; username?: string; }[], priFreq?: number, receiverTankerCHCode?: string, regionCode?: string, regionName?: string, reviewDate?: string, routePoints?: { altCountryCode?: string; countryCode?: string; dafifPt?: boolean; magDec?: number; navaid?: string; navaidLength?: number; navaidType?: string; ptLat?: number; ptLon?: number; ptSequenceId?: number; ptTypeCode?: string; ptTypeName?: string; waypointName?: string; }[], schedulerOrgName?: string, schedulerOrgUnit?: string, secFreq?: number, shortName?: string, sic?: string, trackId?: string, trackName?: string, typeCode?: string): void`\n\n**post** `/udl/trackroute`\n\nService operation to take a single trackroute record as a POST body and ingest into the database. A specific role is required to perform this service operation. Please contact the UDL team for assistance.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `classificationMarking: string`\n  Classification marking of the data in IC/CAPCO Portion-marked format.\n\n- `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  Indicator of whether the data is REAL, TEST, EXERCISE, or SIMULATED data:\n\nREAL: Data collected or produced that pertains to real-world objects, events, and analysis.\n\nTEST: Specific datasets used to evaluate compliance with specifications and requirements, and for validating technical, functional, and performance characteristics.\n\nEXERCISE: Data pertaining to a government or military exercise. The data may include both real and simulated data.\n\nSIMULATED: Synthetic data generated by a model to mimic real-world datasets.\n\n- `lastUpdateDate: string`\n  The last updated date of the track route in ISO 8601 UTC format with millisecond precision.\n\n- `source: string`\n  Source of the data.\n\n- `type: string`\n  The track route type represented by this record (ex. AIR REFUELING).\n\n- `id?: string`\n  Unique identifier of the record, auto-generated by the system.\n\n- `altitudeBlocks?: { altitudeSequenceId?: string; lowerAltitude?: number; upperAltitude?: number; }[]`\n  Minimum and maximum altitude bounds for the track.\n\n- `apnSetting?: string`\n  The APN radar code sent and received by the aircraft for identification.\n\n- `apxBeaconCode?: string`\n  The APX radar code sent and received by the aircraft for identification.\n\n- `artccMessage?: string`\n  Air Refueling Track Control Center message.\n\n- `creatingOrg?: string`\n  The name of the creating organization of the track route.\n\n- `direction?: string`\n  The principal compass direction (cardinal or ordinal) of the track route.\n\n- `effectiveDate?: string`\n  The date which the DAFIF track was last updated/validated in ISO 8601 UTC format with millisecond precision.\n\n- `externalId?: string`\n  Optional air refueling track ID from external systems. This field has no meaning within UDL and is provided as a convenience for systems that require tracking of an internal system generated ID.\n\n- `lastUsedDate?: string`\n  Used to show last time the track route was added to an itinerary in ISO 8601 UTC format with millisecond precision.\n\n- `locationTrackId?: string`\n  Track location ID.\n\n- `origin?: string`\n  Originating system or organization which produced the data, if different from the source. The origin may be different than the source if the source was a mediating system which forwarded the data on behalf of the origin system. If null, the source may be assumed to be the origin.\n\n- `poc?: { office?: string; phone?: string; pocName?: string; pocOrg?: string; pocSequenceId?: number; pocTypeName?: string; rank?: string; remark?: string; username?: string; }[]`\n  Point of contacts for scheduling or modifying the route.\n\n- `priFreq?: number`\n  The primary UHF radio frequency used for the track route in megahertz.\n\n- `receiverTankerCHCode?: string`\n  The receiver tanker channel identifer for air refueling tracks.\n\n- `regionCode?: string`\n  Region code indicating where the track resides as determined by the data source.\n\n- `regionName?: string`\n  Region where the track resides.\n\n- `reviewDate?: string`\n  Date the track needs to be reviewed for accuracy or deletion in ISO 8601 UTC format with millisecond precision.\n\n- `routePoints?: { altCountryCode?: string; countryCode?: string; dafifPt?: boolean; magDec?: number; navaid?: string; navaidLength?: number; navaidType?: string; ptLat?: number; ptLon?: number; ptSequenceId?: number; ptTypeCode?: string; ptTypeName?: string; waypointName?: string; }[]`\n  Points identified within the route.\n\n- `schedulerOrgName?: string`\n  Point of contact for the air refueling track route scheduler.\n\n- `schedulerOrgUnit?: string`\n  The unit responsible for scheduling the track route.\n\n- `secFreq?: number`\n  The secondary UHF radio frequency used for the track route in megahertz.\n\n- `shortName?: string`\n  Abbreviated name of the track.\n\n- `sic?: string`\n  Standard Indicator Code of the air refueling track.\n\n- `trackId?: string`\n  Identifier of the track.\n\n- `trackName?: string`\n  Name of the track.\n\n- `typeCode?: string`\n  Type of process used by AMC to schedule an air refueling event. Possible values are A (Matched Long Range), F (Matched AMC Short Notice), N (Unmatched Theater Operation Short Notice (Theater Assets)), R, Unmatched Long Range, S (Soft Air Refueling), T (Matched Theater Operation Short Notice (Theater Assets)), V (Unmatched AMC Short Notice), X (Unmatched Theater Operation Short Notice (AMC Assets)), Y (Matched Theater Operation Short Notice (AMC Assets)), Z (Other Air Refueling).\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\nawait client.trackRoute.create({\n  classificationMarking: 'U',\n  dataMode: 'TEST',\n  lastUpdateDate: '2024-09-17T16:00:00.123Z',\n  source: 'Bluestaq',\n  type: 'AIR REFUELING',\n})\n```",
