      "## list\n\n`client.vessel.list(firstResult?: number, maxResults?: number): { classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; source: string; id?: string; altVesselId?: string; callsign?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; firstSeen?: string; hullNum?: string; idEntity?: string; idOrganization?: string; imon?: number; length?: number; maxDraught?: number; maxSpeed?: number; mmsi?: string; numBlades?: number; numShafts?: number; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; propType?: string; sconum?: string; status?: string; sternType?: string; vesselBuilder?: string; vesselClass?: string; vesselDescription?: string; vesselFlag?: string; vesselName?: string; vesselType?: string; vslWt?: number; width?: number; yearBuilt?: string; }`\n\n**get** `/udl/vessel`\n\nService operation to dynamically query data by a variety of query parameters not specified in this API documentation. See the queryhelp operation (`/udl/<datatype>/queryhelp`) for more details on valid/required query parameter information.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `firstResult?: number`\n\n- `maxResults?: number`\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ classificationMarking: string; dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'; source: string; id?: string; altVesselId?: string; callsign?: string; createdAt?: string; createdBy?: string; firstSeen?: string; hullNum?: string; idEntity?: string; idOrganization?: string; imon?: number; length?: number; maxDraught?: number; maxSpeed?: number; mmsi?: string; numBlades?: number; numShafts?: number; origin?: string; origNetwork?: string; propType?: string; sconum?: string; status?: string; sternType?: string; vesselBuilder?: string; vesselClass?: string; vesselDescription?: string; vesselFlag?: string; vesselName?: string; vesselType?: string; vslWt?: number; width?: number; yearBuilt?: string; }`\n  This service provides operations for manipulation and querying of maritime Vessel data. Vessel contains the static data of the specific vessel: mmsi, cruise speed, max speed, etc.\n\n  - `classificationMarking: string`\n  - `dataMode: 'REAL' | 'TEST' | 'SIMULATED' | 'EXERCISE'`\n  - `source: string`\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `altVesselId?: string`\n  - `callsign?: string`\n  - `createdAt?: string`\n  - `createdBy?: string`\n  - `firstSeen?: string`\n  - `hullNum?: string`\n  - `idEntity?: string`\n  - `idOrganization?: string`\n  - `imon?: number`\n  - `length?: number`\n  - `maxDraught?: number`\n  - `maxSpeed?: number`\n  - `mmsi?: string`\n  - `numBlades?: number`\n  - `numShafts?: number`\n  - `origin?: string`\n  - `origNetwork?: string`\n  - `propType?: string`\n  - `sconum?: string`\n  - `status?: string`\n  - `sternType?: string`\n  - `vesselBuilder?: string`\n  - `vesselClass?: string`\n  - `vesselDescription?: string`\n  - `vesselFlag?: string`\n  - `vesselName?: string`\n  - `vesselType?: string`\n  - `vslWt?: number`\n  - `width?: number`\n  - `yearBuilt?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Unifieddatalibrary from 'unified-data-library';\n\nconst client = new Unifieddatalibrary();\n\n// Automatically fetches more pages as needed.\nfor await (const vesselListResponse of client.vessel.list()) {\n  console.log(vesselListResponse);\n}\n```",
